---
// Conceptual figure: two input views feed two branches; fusion output looks healthy
// while one branch contributes little. Purely illustrative, no results shown.
---
<figure class="fig">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fd-title fd-desc">
    <title id="fd-title">Silent branch under-utilization</title>
    <desc id="fd-desc">Two input views pass through separate branches into a fusion layer. One branch carries a strong signal; the other contributes little, yet the fused prediction still looks accurate.</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" class="fill-ink" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- inputs -->
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="10" y="40" width="120" height="54" rx="8" />
      <text x="70" y="64">View A</text><text x="70" y="81" class="sub">modality 1</text>
    </g>
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="10" y="156" width="120" height="54" rx="8" />
      <text x="70" y="180">View B</text><text x="70" y="197" class="sub">modality 2</text>
    </g>

    <!-- branches -->
    <g class="node strong">
      <rect x="190" y="40" width="130" height="54" rx="8" />
      <text x="255" y="64">Branch A</text><text x="255" y="81" class="sub">dominates updates</text>
    </g>
    <g class="node faint">
      <rect x="190" y="156" width="130" height="54" rx="8" />
      <text x="255" y="180">Branch B</text><text x="255" y="197" class="sub">learning? ignored?</text>
    </g>

    <!-- fusion + output -->
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="380" y="98" width="100" height="54" rx="8" />
      <text x="430" y="130">Fusion</text>
    </g>
    <g class="node good">
      <rect x="530" y="98" width="100" height="54" rx="8" />
      <text x="580" y="122">Prediction</text><text x="580" y="139" class="sub">high accuracy ✓</text>
    </g>

    <!-- edges -->
    <path d="M130 67H186" class="edge" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
    <path d="M130 183H186" class="edge" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
    <path d="M320 67C350 67 350 115 376 115" class="edge thick" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
    <path d="M320 183C350 183 350 136 376 136" class="edge thin" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
    <path d="M480 125H526" class="edge" marker-end="url(#ah)" />

    <text x="430" y="200" class="q">Is accuracy evidence</text>
    <text x="430" y="216" class="q">that both branches learned?</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Conceptual sketch of the question behind my thesis. It shows the idea only, not results.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig { margin: 0; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .node rect { fill: var(--surface-2); stroke: var(--rule); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .node text { text-anchor: middle; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--text); }
  .node text.sub { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 400; fill: var(--muted); }
  .node.strong rect { stroke: var(--accent); fill: var(--accent-soft); }
  .node.faint rect { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .node.faint text { opacity: 0.6; }
  .node.good rect { stroke: var(--ok); }
  .node.good text.sub { fill: var(--ok); }
  .edge { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-2); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .edge.thick { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 4; }
  .edge.thin { stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 4; opacity: 0.6; }
  .fill-ink { fill: var(--text-2); }
  .q { text-anchor: middle; font-size: 12px; font-style: italic; fill: var(--muted); font-family: var(--font-serif); }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
